{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on 0dc7c1e9 for the cutover head (05d618e2).\n\nQ-S4. The constant names the last commit of `main` before the\ncutover lands, as 40 hex characters. Keep it out of\npackages/contract: it is a fact of one deployment, not a term of\nthe protocol. Put it in the lowest package that both\nscope/src/room-retired.ts and mcp/src/store-format-error.ts\nalready import, other than contract, and name that package in the\nnote. You write the value when I open the hold on `main` for this\nhead. The gate runs after that, and `main` does not move until the\nhead lands. The store-format refusal returns `Said` with that text\nand no extra fields.\n\nQ-GP. Choose (a). genesis-proof.ts admits a foreign entry by its\nbody and by the content digest of the retained use that names it.\nThe scope's own entry recorded that use when it read the entry, so\nthe own entry is the authority. Ruling 222a5b21 adds no read.\n\nV1. Confirmed. command-verify.ts compares the page's reference\nwith `config.register`. Compare the full reference where the\nconfig holds one.\n\n10b gap. If the directory read that the page already makes\nreturns the partition references, the page keeps them, and the\nrow locks the directory and reads \"in this room\" as before. That\nadds no request. If that read does not return them, accept the\ngap, and tell me. I then file a follow-up for the read.\n\nWorkspace host. Confirmed, on the reasoning of Q-GP. The exported\nname and its comment say that it proves the body and the digest\nand no address. No caller treats its result as proof of an\naddress.\n\nCensus config. A `v: 2` config is part of this head. Ruling\ne46dd964, item 5, says so: packages/cli/src/files.ts writes\n`v: 2`, accepts 2 and nothing else, and refuses a `v: 1` home with\nthe stated message before any signing. files.ts:107 still tests\nfor 1 at 5278e142. The census command reads the same config, so\nit expects 2. `dap mcp` gives the same refusal.\n\nRuling 9 seeds. The two seed digests are allowed. Ruling 9\nforbids a made-up genesis digest in place of an admitted genesis.\nA seed is an input, and the genesis that the helper makes from it\nis real bytes. Give each distinct stand-in its own seed.\n\nThe registry revert waits until the source compiles, as you say.\nThe table of 125 dropped checks is noted. I read it when the head\nis in review.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}